 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the real property tax law, in relation to subjecting the\nCaumsett State Historic Park Preserve and Planting Fields Arboretum State\nHistoric Park to taxation for all purposes",
    "basePrintNo": "S981",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S981-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §532, RPT L",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Tax Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S981\n\nSPONSOR: GAUGHRAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the real property tax law, in relation to subjecting the\nCaumsett State Historic Park Preserve and Planting Fields Arboretum\nState Historic Park to taxation for all purposes\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill relates to subjecting the Caumsett State Historic park\nPreserve and Planting Fields Arboretum State Historic Park to taxation\nfor all purposes\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill adds Caumsett State Historic Park Preserve in the\ncounty of Suffolk, and Planting Fields Arboretum State Historic Park in\nthe county of Nassau, to the tax rolls.\n\nSection 2 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPlanting Field Arboretum State Historic Park accounts for 13 percent of\nland within the Village of Upper Brookville, and Caumsett State Historic\nPark Preserve accounts for 35 percent of land within the Village of\nLloyd Harbor. A large portion of emergency response calls for these\nmunicipalities are to their corresponding state parks, costing taxpayers\nwithout any reimbursement. This is valuable land for which the State\ncollects revenue; the State should share some of the proceeds of the\nrevenue with its host communities to lessen the financial burden on\nlocal property tax owners.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019-20: S6026A\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nPositive implications to be determined.\n\n \nIMPACT ON REGULATION OF BUSINESS AND INDIVIDUALS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECT ON FINES, TERMS OF IMPRISONMENT OR OTHER PENAL SANCTIONS;\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on April 1, 2021.\n",
